            "properties": {
                "0": {
                    "name": "block",
                    "value": "The construct_dict node gathers several inlets into one dictionary.\n\nIts arguments are the keys: \"construct_dict x y\" has an x inlet and a y inlet. Fill them in any order, then click 'send dict' (or send anything to it) and the dictionary goes out - one bundle carrying every value under its name.\n\ngather_to_dict is another name for the same node.\n\nWHAT IS KEPT BETWEEN SENDS:\nThe inlets named by the arguments keep their last value, so each send includes every one of them - a key whose inlet has never received anything is sent with no value. Entries added through 'labelled data in' are cleared after each send.\n\nADDING ENTRIES AT RUN TIME:\n'labelled data in' takes a list whose first element is the key. The rest of the list becomes the value, and is always a list - \"speed 3\" files the list 3, not the number 3. A key that is also an argument is overwritten by that argument's inlet when the dictionary is sent.\n\nSYNTAX:\nconstruct_dict <key> <key> ...\ngather_to_dict <key> <key> ...\n\nEXAMPLE:\nconstruct_dict x y confidence\n\nINPUTS and PARAMETERS:\n\nsend dict:\nSends the dictionary.\n\n<one inlet per key>:\nThe value for that key. Arriving here does not send anything.\n\nlabelled data in:\nA key followed by its value, added to the next dictionary only.\n\nOUTPUTS:\n\ndict out:\nThe dictionary.\n\nRELATED:\ndict_extract takes a dictionary apart again, one outlet per key. dict is a store you add to and look up from.",
                    "value_type": "str"
                },
                "1": {
                    "name": "lock",
                    "value": true,
                    "value_type": "bool"
                },
                "2": {
                    "name": "width",
                    "value": 800,
                    "value_type": "int"
                },
                "3": {
                    "name": "height",
                    "value": 700,
                    "value_type": "int"
                },
                "4": {
                    "name": "text_size",
                    "value": "30",
                    "value_type": "str"
                }
            },
            "text": "The construct_dict node gathers several inlets into one dictionary.\n\nIts arguments are the keys: \"construct_dict x y\" has an x inlet and a y inlet. Fill them in any order, then click 'send dict' (or send anything to it) and the dictionary goes out - one bundle carrying every value under its name.\n\ngather_to_dict is another name for the same node.\n\nWHAT IS KEPT BETWEEN SENDS:\nThe inlets named by the arguments keep their last value, so each send includes every one of them - a key whose inlet has never received anything is sent with no value. Entries added through 'labelled data in' are cleared after each send.\n\nADDING ENTRIES AT RUN TIME:\n'labelled data in' takes a list whose first element is the key. The rest of the list becomes the value, and is always a list - \"speed 3\" files the list 3, not the number 3. A key that is also an argument is overwritten by that argument's inlet when the dictionary is sent.\n\nSYNTAX:\nconstruct_dict <key> <key> ...\ngather_to_dict <key> <key> ...\n\nEXAMPLE:\nconstruct_dict x y confidence\n\nINPUTS and PARAMETERS:\n\nsend dict:\nSends the dictionary.\n\n<one inlet per key>:\nThe value for that key. Arriving here does not send anything.\n\nlabelled data in:\nA key followed by its value, added to the next dictionary only.\n\nOUTPUTS:\n\ndict out:\nThe dictionary.\n\nRELATED:\ndict_extract takes a dictionary apart again, one outlet per key. dict is a store you add to and look up from."
        },
